message: "If you use NodeSubstrates in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NodeSubstrates: Bridging Node-Link Diagrams with DR-Based Semantic Substrates"
authors:
  - family-names: Vink
    given-names: Sjoerd
  - family-names: Christino
    given-names: Leonardo
  - family-names: Behrisch
    given-names: Michael
year: 2026
publisher: "The Eurographics Association"
conference: "EuroVis 2026"
abstract: >
  Multivariate graph visualization faces a fundamental tension between representing
  network topology and showing attribute-driven structure. Existing techniques force
  analysts to choose between these perspectives, hindering the inspection of
  attribute-defined groupings within their structural context. Node-link diagrams
  convey connectivity but obscure attribute relationships, while dimensionality
  reduction projections expose attribute similarity at the cost of explicit edge
  information. We present NodeSubstrates, a hybrid visualization technique that
  integrates node-link diagrams with DR-based semantic substrates. Nodes are
  selectively repositioned using dimensionality reduction on their attributes,
  revealing clusters and outliers not visible in topological layouts. Substrate
  regions can be interactively created and dissolved. We demonstrate NodeSubstrates
  on real-world data, showing how the hybrid representation supports tasks spanning
  attributes and graph structure.
license: MIT
